{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 7,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not an appointed time to man upon earth? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are not",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his days also like the days of a hireling?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As a servant earnestly desireth the shadow, and as a hireling looketh for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the reward of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his work;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So am I made to possess months of vanity, and wearisome nights are appointed to me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When I lie down, I say, When shall I arise, and the night be gone? and I am full of tossings to and fro to the dawning of the day.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My flesh is clothed with worms and clods of dust; my skin is broken and become lothsome.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My days are swifter than a weaver's shuttle, and are spent without hope.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O remember that my life ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wind: my eye will no more see good.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The eye of him that hath seen me shall see me no ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "more",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": thy eyes ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon me, and I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the cloud is consumed and vanisheth away: so he that goeth down to the grave shall come up no ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "more",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall return no more to his house, neither shall his place know him any more.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore I will not restrain my mouth; I will speak in the anguish of my spirit; I will complain in the bitterness of my soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I a sea, or a whale, that thou settest a watch over me?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When I say, My bed shall comfort me, my couch shall ease my complaint;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then thou scarest me with dreams, and terrifiest me through visions:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So that my soul chooseth strangling, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " death rather than my life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I lothe ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; I would not live always: let me alone; for my days ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vanity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " man, that thou shouldst magnify him? and that thou shouldst set thy heart upon him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou shouldst visit him every morning, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " try him every moment?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How long wilt thou not depart from me, nor let me alone till I swallow my spittle?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have sinned; what shall I do to thee, O thou preserver of men? why hast thou set me as a mark against thee, so that I am a burden to myself?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.7.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.7.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And why dost thou not pardon my transgression, and take away my iniquity? for now shall I sleep in the dust; and thou shalt seek me in the morning, but I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
